YOUR TASK: Complete this task: Implement the complete Python program for the pairwise-bad-pair solution and verify it. Use l=min(S,T), r=max(S,T), sign=0 if S<T else 1. Compute the earliest later bad partner for each person: (1) backward scan for same l or same r; (2) for same-sign crossing, run an increasing-index sweep for each sign on original coordinates and on mirrored coordinates (l'=N+1-r, r'=N+1-l). In each sweep maintain a segment tree over right endpoints where each leaf is a min-heap of encoded (left,index) for active earlier intervals of that sign; for current interval [L,R], extract all active earlier intervals with L < r_i < R and l_i < L, set their crossing partner to the current index, then insert the current interval. Take the elementwise minimum of all partner sources, build a suffix minimum, and answer query [L,R] with Yes iff suffix[L] > R. Use strict open ranges, separate signs, and test on both samples plus a separate small random brute-force difference-constraints checker that includes touching endpoints.